# Secrets for local development. Copy this file to .dev.vars (which git ignores), remove the "# " in front of a
# secret and fill it in. On Cloudflare, add each one with `npx wrangler secret put NAME`, or in the dashboard
# (Workers & Pages > your game > Settings > Variables and Secrets). Never commit a real value.
# Both secrets are optional, so they stay comments here: the "Deploy to Cloudflare" setup page asks for every
# secret in this file and does not go on while one is empty. Add them later (README, step 4).
# An empty value and `none` both mean "not set".

# Optional but advised: a Nano node API key, for example Nanswap Nodes (https://nanswap.com/nano-node).
# Read the provider's terms first: some free keys are for personal use only.
# Payments are checked there first, then on public Nano nodes.
# NODE_API_KEY=

# Optional: the secret key of a Cloudflare Turnstile widget (its site key is TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY).
# TURNSTILE_SECRET=

# Optional: the client secret that Nanoterra shows once on its launch page (the client id goes in NANOTERRA_CLIENT_ID in
# wrangler.jsonc). It lets a player who is signed in at Nanoterra arrive here signed in. Never put it in a page or a log.
# NANOTERRA_SECRET=
